# DrumPadMachine

Kotlin, multi-module Gradle (Kotlin DSL, **no version catalog** — deps live
only in `buildSrc/src/main/kotlin/ApplicationDependencies*.kt`, add new ones
there). Jetpack Compose + Material3 (no XML layouts). Dagger Hilt DI. Room DB.
Retrofit/OkHttp/Gson. `compose-destinations` nav (generated `NavGraphs` —
don't hand-write). Firebase Crashlytics/Analytics. Native audio via Oboe/JNI.

## Modules
- `:app` (`com.slaviboy.drumpadmachine`) — feature-first:
  `screens/<feature>/{composables,viewmodels,helpers,usecases}` for
  `drumpad`/`home`/`lessonslist`/`presetslist`; `data/room/<entity>/` one
  folder per table (`*Entity.kt` + `*Dao.kt`); `data/entities/` domain
  models; `data/workers/` CoroutineWorkers; `api/` Retrofit
  repos/services; `modules/` Hilt modules.
- `:lib:audio` — Kotlin/JNI bridge, `DrumPadPlayer.kt`
  (trigger/stopTrigger/pan/gain/loadWav*).
- `:lib:oboe`, `:lib:iolib`, `:lib:parselib` — native C++, edit with care,
  needs NDK/CMake 3.22.1. Prefer changing `:lib:audio` over native code
  unless the task requires it.

## Pattern
MVVM + Repository, `@HiltViewModel` injects repositories. Namespace =
`com.slaviboy.<module>`.

## Domain core
`DrumPadPlayer` (native audio wrapper) + `DrumPadViewModel`
(`screens/drumpad/viewmodels/`, multi-touch hit-testing, choke groups, pad
paging) are the heart of pad/audio behavior. `Preset`/`File` entities hold
pad config (filename, color, choke, stopOnRelease). Resource load order:
DB → extracted ZIP → API ZIP, synced via `CoroutineWorker` into Room.

## Facts to stop re-deriving
- No tests exist (`app/src/test`, `androidTest` absent) — don't search for
  them.
- No CI (`.github/` absent).
- Build variants: `dev`/`beta`/`prod` × debug/release, e.g.
  `./gradlew assembleDevDebug`.

## Conventions
Follow the existing feature-first / per-entity-folder shape for new code
instead of inventing a new structure. Don't grep `build.gradle.kts` files for
dependency versions — check `buildSrc` instead.
